-- The flag of the Republic of South Africa
-- Constitution of the Republic of South Africa 1996, Schedule 1.
-- Architecture: Tom Dyer.
-- First script and colours: Gemini (it stopped at line 22: 'mark' is not a shape).
-- These words: Claude (Opus 5.5).
--
-- The flag is 2 high and 3 long, so "one fifth as wide as the flag" is 2/5,
-- "one fifteenth" is 2/15 and "one third" is 2/3.

colour sagreen is #007749
colour sagold  is #ffb81c
colour sablack is #000000
colour sawhite is #ffffff
colour sared   is #e03c31
colour sablue  is #001489

make south africa flag
  size 3 by 2
  -- clause 6: red above, blue below
  paint all sared
  box sablue from 0 1 to 3 2
  -- clause 3: the centre lines of the band start in the top and bottom
  -- corners next to the flag post, meet in the middle, then go to the fly.
  -- clause 4: white edges, each 2/15. Green 2/5 + two white 2/15 = 2/3.
  band sawhite from top left to middle thick 2/3
  band sawhite from bottom left to middle thick 2/3
  band sawhite from middle to right thick 2/3
  -- clause 4: on the flag post side the edge is gold, not white.
  -- Its middle is 1/5 + 1/15 = 4/15 from the centre line, on the inside.
  band sagold from middle to top left thick 2/15 shift 4/15 left
  band sagold from bottom left to middle thick 2/15 shift 4/15 left
  -- clause 3: the green band, one fifth as wide as the flag
  band sagreen from top left to middle thick 2/5
  band sagreen from bottom left to middle thick 2/5
  band sagreen from middle to right thick 2/5
  -- clause 5: the black triangle. Its sides are 1/3 inside each centre line.
  -- The corners need the root of 13: 0.400617 is root 13 / 9,
  -- and 0.899074 is 3/2 less root 13 / 6.
  shape sablack from 0 0.400617 to 0.899074 1 to 0 1.599383
end

page 1200 wide
draw south africa flag
